 "notes": "ACCESS: ashleyfurniture.com sits behind PerimeterX. The mobile curl_cffi profile safari18_0_ios (per the prior Home-Decor pass) worked for the first ~10 requests - it delivered robots.txt, the sitemap index, the category sitemap and the full server-rendered mega-menu - and then this IP was captcha'd for the rest of the session (15-profile sweep: every chrome/safari/edge/firefox desktop profile plus both iOS and android profiles returned 403 px-captcha). All remaining pages were read through r.jina.ai, which is unrestricted here; note that plain python-requests reaches jina while curl_cffi impersonation gets a Cloudflare challenge from jina itself. robots.txt names no anthropic-ai / ClaudeBot / Claude-Web agent and does not disallow /c/ category paths. TREE: taken from the site's own server-rendered mega-menu (11 top-level departments, embedded in every page's HTML), cross-checked against sitemap_7-category.xml (1,991 category URLs, 732 of them under /c/furniture/). QTY: every number is the storefront's own rendered listing header - the #product-results element, e.g. '1 - 30 of 356 products'. The site also emits a SECOND header inside .mobile-product-count that is sometimes 1-2 higher (sofas 356 vs 357, beds 500 vs 502); the desktop #product-results value was used throughout, which matches the prior Home-Decor pass on this site. SANITY CHECKS: the one page fetched both ways (sofas) gave 356 on the direct curl_cffi read and 356 through jina - identical. Eight leaves were read a second time (beds 500, outdoor bar stools 55, dining chairs 460, kids beds 204, desks 156, TV stands 501, bathroom vanities 34, cribs 136) and every one matched its first read. The two suspiciously round/large numbers were confirmed by paging to the true end: beds ?start=480 renders '481 - 500 of 500 products' and accent tables ?start=720 renders '721 - 735 of 735 products', so neither is a display cap. Counts differ per category, so no site-wide constant is being echoed. Each leaf's h1 was checked against the category it was meant to be. EXCLUDED: mattresses and all mattress / bed-and-mattress sets (bedding, not furniture); bedding, rugs, textiles, throw pillows, poufs, window treatments; lighting and ceiling fans; mirrors including floor mirrors; wall art and wall decor; home accents, vases, clocks, sculptures, artificial plants; bathroom fixtures and bathroom mirrors; fire pits, fire-pit tables and patio heating (heating appliances); patio umbrellas, outdoor cushions and pillows, furniture covers, outdoor decor; garage and closet-organiser storage; baby gear, strollers, play mats. Dropped as navigation / marketing / filter pages: the several hundred named Collections slugs, Deals / Price Cuts / Outlet / Clearance / Labor Day, New Arrivals, Best Sellers, Shop By Style / Color / Room / Look, the Small Spaces and Large Spaces roll-ups, Performance Fabric and Leather Seating (material filters), Mirrored Dressers (finish filter), Extendable Dining Tables (feature filter), the coffee-table shape/material children (black, glass, marble, round, square, wood, lift-top, storage, modern), the bed size/style children (twin, full, queen, king, cal-king, panel, platform, sleigh, canopy, upholstered, metal, four-poster, storage), the dining-set children (counter-height, dinette, dining-nook), and Shop By Gender (girls / boys / gender-neutral). PARENTS TURNED INTO GROUPING ROWS because they have extractable children: Reclining Furniture, Modular Furniture (400), Dressers & Chests of Drawers (400) over Dressers 297 + Chests of Drawers 158, Bedroom Storage (195), Dining Storage (286), Kids Dressers & Chests (164) over Kids Dressers 121 + Kids Chests 54, Outdoor Seating (777), Outdoor Tables (274), Outdoor Dining Furniture (591), Outdoor Bar Furniture (118). DELIBERATE OMISSIONS: /c/furniture/living-room/storage/ (240) was dropped because its child Accent Cabinets (347) is the mega-menu leaf and is larger than the parent; /c/outdoor/outdoor-sets/patio-sets/ (6